🚀 Git Notes (Beginner → Intermediate)
📌 1. Basic Git Workflow
git init            → Initialize a new repository
git add .           → Stage all files
git commit -m ""    → Create a commit
git status          → Check changes
git log             → View commit history
git log --oneline   → Short log

📌 2. Inspecting Commits
View one commit
git show <commit-id>

View only file names changed
git show --name-only <commit-id>

Show reflog (all HEAD movements)
git reflog

📌 3. Branching & Switching
git branch                → Show branches
git branch <name>         → Create branch
git checkout <name>       → Switch to branch
git checkout -b <name>    → Create + switch

📌 4. Merging Branches
Merge FeatureBranch into main:
git checkout main
git merge FeatureBranch


This creates a merge commit.

📌 5. Working with Remote (GitHub)
Set remote upstream on first push
git push --set-upstream origin main

Regular push/pull
git push
git pull

Clone a repo
git clone <url>

📌 6. How git revert works (SAFE undo)
Used to undo commits that are ALREADY pushed.

It creates a new commit that reverses the changes of an older commit.

Example from your workflow:

You reverted the commit test commit.

git revert 743a59a


This created:

Revert "test commit"
This reverts commit 743a59a...


✔ Original commit stays in history
✔ A new commit removes the file
✔ Safe for teamwork

📌 7. How git reset works (DANGEROUS undo)
Used to move HEAD to an older commit.
Rewrites history.

You used:

git reset b2c80cd


Now your history became:

Initial commit → Main branch commit


The revert and the "test commit" disappeared from your local branch.

⚠ If you push after reset:

git push --force


This overwrites GitHub history — dangerous for shared repos.

📌 8. Types of Reset
1. Soft Reset (keeps staging files)
git reset --soft <commit>

2. Mixed Reset (default — keeps working directory, unstages files)
git reset <commit>

3. Hard Reset (deletes all local changes)
git reset --hard <commit>

📌 9. Git Checkout Examples (your workflow)
Switch to branch
git checkout FeatureBranch

Go back to main
git checkout main

📌 10. Compare reset vs revert (FINAL SUMMARY)
Feature	git reset	git revert
Undo style	Deletes commits	Creates new opposite commit
Safe for pushed commits?	❌ No	✔ Yes
Rewrites history?	✔ Yes	❌ No
Use case	Local mistakes	Team-safe undo
