📌 12. Important Command Meanings
Command	Meaning
git add	Moves files to staging area
git reset <file>	Removes file from staging (unstages)
git reset <commit>	Moves HEAD to older commit
git revert <commit>	Creates commit that undoes changes
git checkout <branch>	Switches branch
git merge <branch>	Combines branch into current one
git reflog	Shows every HEAD movement
git show <commit>	Shows patch (changes) of one commit
git show --name-only	Shows only changed filenames
git push	Upload to GitHub
git pull	Download & merge from GitHub
